# najamjad - COUNTED series. Identical contract to the friendly, and separate
# ONLY because of where the report goes. Read config/opponents/najamjad.env for
# why every line below is what it is; nothing is re-argued here.
#
#   scripts/play.sh najamjad-counted --role police --counted --prior-counted 6
#
# THE TWO FLAGS ARE NOT OPTIONAL AND NOT IN THIS FILE, because neither is an
# environment variable:
#
#   --counted          enforces the binding six sub-games and turns on the
#                      typed confirmation and the clean-tree refusal.
#   --prior-counted 6  our truthful rule-37 count. We omitted it in the
#                      2026-08-20 warm-up and step-0 declared nothing, so
#                      najamjad's filed artifact recorded `ahk-yosi: 0` while
#                      we had told them 6 in writing. Harmless in a friendly;
#                      in a counted series that is the rule-38 disagreement
#                      between two files that rules 33-35 void a series over.
#                      The number is the count of counted archives in matches/
#                      (orcai-mj, amireman/G012, saedshki, s82kma9e, gal-roy1,
#                      uoh-ay26) and README section 16 is the running record.
#
# BLOCKED until we run two processes. najamjad accepted our single process for
# the WARM-UP only, in writing on 2026-08-20: "Rule 1 binds a counted series; a
# warm-up files nothing, so there is nothing for it to bind on. Before anything
# counted we'd want the split." So this file is ready and the match is not.
#
# Warm-up result 2026-08-20: 90-30, 6-0, all six audits Verified OK, mutual
# signature f77e4fb9... agreed byte-for-byte by both sides.

P2P_DIALECT=reference
P2P_ALTERNATE_ROLES=true

# A FRESH negotiate opens every mini-game on their side; a peer that holds one
# session for the series leaves them waiting at every handover. Their words:
# "One evening was lost to exactly this."
P2P_HANDSHAKE_PER_SUB_GAME=true

# SCENT: A2, subtractive_chebyshev_v1, both sides emitting.
#
# Not a preference - the only option that can start. Their book document is the
# kit's registered one (934c220d...) and ours is our own (ea7225f5...), so a
# book series would refuse at the handshake on `check_compatibility`'s scent
# lock. Both sides adopted the kit's SUBTRACTIVE document byte-for-byte, so
# those two digests are identical and A2 binds:
#     81ebee59640e80eae8ca9ee5f86abd26e7edf5cdbb27d15925cb6ee45ca6ddf4
# Their accumulation is a max-merge against the 0.9 ceiling; so is ours under
# this model (`scent_subtractive.emit`). Under book ours is additive-then-clamp
# and would have diverged above the ceiling - a second reason A2 is the clean
# one. Confirmed live on their side, not merely intended.
P2P_SCENT_MODEL=subtractive_chebyshev_v1
# Physics and doctrine are ONE decision in two variables, and the second half is
# easy to forget - `test_doctrine_per_physics` caught this line missing from
# this very file. A subtractive field is a SHORT memory (the outer ring is gone
# in three steps), so trail-age reasoning tuned on multiplicative traces reads it
# wrong: measured at roughly two thirds of our captures against uoh-sqak.
P2P_DOCTRINE=config/doctrine-subtractive.json

# SERVE ORDER: cut the packet BEFORE the decay, so our freshest centre reads
# 0.9 / 0.6 / 0.3 rather than 0.8 / 0.5 / 0.2.
#
# The lock document pins `order: deposit_then_decay` for the GRID and never
# says which side of the decay the packet is cut from, so both readings hash to
# 81ebee59... and the digest cannot separate them - only this line can. We read
# it the late way and s82kma9e's two golden served fields require the late way,
# which is what we filed a counted series under; najamjad read the same document
# the early way. Theirs is the better reading of intent: an opponent that decodes
# intensity as age is otherwise handed a systematic one-step lag, and in the
# 2026-08-20 friendly their police stood on the cell our thief had just left 3
# times per window and made exactly one capture claim, for the cell we had
# vacated one step earlier.
#
# They verify our first transmitted grid peaks at 0.9 and stop the series at
# step 1 if it does not. PER-OPPONENT and never global: flipping the default
# would put us out of conformance with s82kma9e's published vectors and with a
# counted result already filed.
P2P_SCENT_SERVE_BEFORE_DECAY=true

# ENCLOSURE CLAIM OFF, at their request and on their reasoning: rule 47 wants
# the thief's confirmation, and a capture the thief never acknowledges is a
# rules 33-35 void for BOTH teams - strictly worse for us than the survival we
# declined. Their thief concedes on its own turn when it has no legal move, so
# waiting costs us nothing. If it ever fails to concede where it should, raise
# it with them rather than closing the game unilaterally.
P2P_CLAIM_ENCLOSURE=false

# PATIENCE: 1000 s per window, both sides, agreed explicitly.
#
# Ours was 180/90, far under theirs, which made US the side that manufactures
# the failure: whichever peer runs out first is indistinguishable from a broken
# opponent. Their own figure is bounded on WALL CLOCK rather than attempts,
# after they found that "attempts x backoff" understated a door that times out
# rather than refuses by roughly an order of magnitude.
P2P_HANDSHAKE_BUDGET=1000
P2P_REHANDSHAKE_BUDGET=1000

# RE-OFFER A FAILED WINDOW under its own number rather than advancing past it.
# Their §3.1, and they chose it when we offered to conform either way: two peers
# advancing at different rates ended three of their series on consecutive
# evenings, with one side on window 5 while the other held 3 and every window
# after refused by both guards. Bounded at 2 so a genuinely dead peer still ends
# the series. Default is 0 everywhere else - a peer that does not re-offer would
# read our replay of N as a stale duplicate.
P2P_WINDOW_REOFFERS=2

# Their two permanent doors, one per role they hold. Our police dials their
# thief and our thief dials their cop; `retarget_link` flips at every boundary.
P2P_OPPONENT_COP_URL=https://cop.4laboratory.com/mcp
P2P_OPPONENT_THIEF_URL=https://thief.4laboratory.com/mcp

# NO series-consensus exchange: their contract does not specify the §10.3
# digest, and it rides on submit_audit - a peer that does not expect it there
# sees an audit package with no records, which turns a clean series into a
# technical loss on their side.
P2P_SERIES_CONSENSUS=false

# NO game_id label. Their §6 derives it as "<lo>-vs-<hi>" with no label slot,
# and game_id is the FIRST signed key of mutual_agreement.sha256 - a label on
# one side only guarantees a digest mismatch at the end of a clean series.
# Both sides must land on:
#     game_id  ahk-yosi-vs-najamjad
#     game_uid c581764c-4c29-50a6-f800-a5d416ef9536
# (Deliberately unset rather than set empty: P2P_GAME_ID is only read when
# non-empty, so leaving it out is what "derive it" means.)

# -- EMAIL: THE LECTURER, and this is the only line that differs from the
# friendly contract ------------------------------------------------------------
# Counted results go to rmisegal+uoh26finalgame@gmail.com, from EACH team
# separately (their section 7.4 and ours agree). Set explicitly rather than left
# to the committed game.toml default, so this file states its own destination
# and cannot be changed by an edit somewhere else.
#
# play.sh REFUSES the reverse mistake - a friendly whose report would reach the
# lecturer - because a friendly filed there reads as THE counted encounter and
# the book allows exactly one per pair.
P2P_EMAIL_MODE=send
P2P_EMAIL_RECIPIENT=rmisegal+uoh26finalgame@gmail.com

# OUR public doors, per role, published in the identity block so their handshake
# recovery can re-send its agreement to the right one. These are quick-tunnel
# hostnames and die with the tunnel process - RE-EXPORT THEM AND RE-SEND THEM TO
# najamjad BEFORE EVERY RUN. Left here as a template, not as live values:
#   export P2P_PUBLIC_COP_URL=https://<police-tunnel>/mcp    # our port 8802
#   export P2P_PUBLIC_THIEF_URL=https://<thief-tunnel>/mcp   # our port 8801
#
# Without them the identity block falls back to http://0.0.0.0:<port>/mcp, which
# is unreachable and names one door for both roles.

# Zero-token banter. We told them our per-turn envelope stays well inside their
# 30 s deadline; the LLM provider has a 30 s step deadline of its own and could
# push a single turn against it. This is what makes that promise true.
P2P_TRASH_TALK_PROVIDER=template
